^SAMPLE = GSM3636016
!Sample_title = ANTI-CD22-4
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM3636016
!Sample_status = Public on Mar 01 2019
!Sample_submission_date = Feb 28 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = Mar 01 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = microglia
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain: C57BL/6
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: 18 months old
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = To assess the transcriptional effects of CD22 blockade, we implanted aged mice with osmotic pumps to continuously infuse a CD22 blocking antibody or an IgG control antibody directly into the cerebrospinal fluid for one month. Following one month of continuous infusion, we performed RNA-seq on purified microglia from the hemi-brains of these mice contralateral to the cannulation site to minimize injury-induced confounding factors.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Primary mouse microglia were isolated by gentle dounce homogenization of the brain, magentic myelin removal, and FACS-purification of ~20,000 live CD11b+CD45lo cells. Microglia were sorted into RLT Plus buffer (Qiagen) containing beta-mercaptoethanol. RNA was extracted using a RNeasy Micro Plus kit (Qiagen) according the manufacturer’s protocol. RNA integrity was assessed on a Bioanalyzer (Agilent), and high quality samples were used for library preparation.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = cDNA synthesis and amplification was performed using the SmartSeq v4 Ultra-low input kit (Takara), and libraries were tagmented, adaptor ligated, and indexed using the Nextera XT kit (Illumina). After normalization and pooling, libraries were sequenced on a Hiseq 4000 (Illumina) using paired-end 100bp reads.
!Sample_data_processing = bcl2fastq
!Sample_data_processing = STAR
!Sample_data_processing = SummarizedExperiment
!Sample_data_processing = DESeq2
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: .csv normalized counts
